# Seed Rules

Seeds create or reconcile data. They must be managed separately from migrations.

## Required Practices

- Keep seed scripts in explicit seed folders or journey folders.
- Make seeds idempotent by checking stable business keys before insert.
- Wrap multi-step seeds in transactions when possible.
- Separate foundation/reference seeds from demo, journey, and e2e seeds.
- Document which environments may run each seed.
- Make cleanup behavior explicit when cleanup exists.

## Prohibited Practices

- Do not change schema in seeds.
- Do not rely on migrations to insert demo or e2e data.
- Do not use random identifiers when a stable key is needed for idempotency.
- Do not run destructive seed cleanup outside controlled environments.

## Review Checklist

- The seed can run twice without duplicating data.
- The target environment is clear.
- The seed depends on migrations having already run.
- The seed avoids hard-coded production secrets.
